OL,3,GNEWSAKetamine is 'leaving people in
OL,4,Anappies', warns deputy mayor
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe deputy mayor of West Yorkshire says
OL,7,Fthe effects of taking ketamine can be
OL,8,F"catastrophic" - and tackling it is one
OL,9,Fof her priorities.
OL,11,FBaroness Alison Lowe, who oversees
OL,12,Fpolicing and crime, has been answering
OL,13,Fquestions on Message the Mayor on BBC
OL,14,FRadio Leeds.
OL,16,FThe deputy mayor was also asked about
OL,17,Fknife crime, the number of police
OL,18,Fofficers who have been barred, and her
OL,19,Fown future.
OL,21,FYou can read our takeaways below, or
OL,22,Flisten to the full interview here.
